  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Volunteers can note busy garden paths and schedule small maintenance tasks without closing the garden.\", \"decision\": \"How should path maintenance respond to visitor use?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers observe visitor use before choosing path-maintenance times. Maintenance can avoid the periods when a path is busiest.\nVolunteers announce path-maintenance times and ask visitors to suggest adjustments before work begins. A proposed schedule is checked against visitors’ plans.\nVolunteers maintain one path at a time while directing visitors to another observed route. Access continues through a changing available route."
    }
